{:adr/id "2607121900"
 :adr/title "implement the raycast host binding (Phase A1 of ADR-2607121800)"
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/date "2026-07-12"
 :adr/related ["2607121800-network-isekai-aaa-nintendo-quality-roadmap"
               "2607100030-kotoba-kami-engine-host-imports"]

 :gap "kotoba.engine-clj.ast declares raycast in the WASM host-import ABI (kami:engine/physics@1.0.0/raycast, 6xf32 in / i64 out) but kami.host (kotoba-lang/host's browser ECS host) never implemented it -- a guest calling it got a WebAssembly.instantiate LinkError. Blocked any aimed-hitscan gameplay. Also found kami.host.cljc's own (:require [kami.physics :as phys]) was a pre-existing bug -- kotoba-lang/physics only provides kotoba.physics -- which made the whole namespace fail to load, so this repo's own test suite was not actually running before this change."

 :decision "implement raycast as a ray-vs-sphere nearest-hit scan over the ECS (:ents map), same O(n) idiom as the existing :nearest import, along a ray instead of within a radius of a point. Fixed constants raycast-hit-radius (120) / raycast-max-range (6000) since the ECS stores no per-entity render size and the ABI has no room for extra params. Untargeted by design (no tag filter in the ABI) -- can hit scenery/structures too, which is correct (walls block shots); callers cross-check nearest-tagged for a specific tag, compare against their own id to exclude self. apply-force! stays a no-op (no caller yet). Fixed the kami.physics -> kotoba.physics require bug alongside it."

 :verification {:jvm-tests "clojure -M:test in kotoba-lang/host: 3 tests / 5 assertions, 0 failures (previously did not load at all)"
                :browser "raycast's actual hit math is #?(:cljs ...)-gated; verified end-to-end as part of ADR-2607121800 Phase B (a hitscan weapon actually damages/kills a bot in a real browser build)"}

 :consequences ["hitscan combat and aimed build-placement are now fully guest-authorable (raycast + nearest-tagged + spawn/despawn + defatom health) -- no further host capability needed for those specifically"
                "travelling-projectile combat was already fully expressible before this change (spawn-entity + set-velocity! + nearest-tagged), unaffected"
                "raycast-hit-radius/-max-range are fixed, not per-call -- a future game needing a very different hit radius would need either a new ABI revision or to tolerate the shared default; flagged as a known limitation, not a blocker"]}
